{"availability":"available","full":"Kosmoray/dayan-motion-atlas","name":"dayan-motion-atlas","description":"32 semantic motion patterns for AI-built presentations. Meaning first.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-28T11:01:32Z","updated":"2026-10-09T10:06:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kosmoray.github.io/dayan-motion-atlas/","topics":["ai-presentations","animation","css-animation","github-pages","motion-design","semantic-motion"],"demo":"https://kosmoray.github.io/dayan-motion-atlas/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:11:29.051Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T07:11:29.051Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T07:11:29.051Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:05:20.885Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T07:11:29.051Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A visual decision system for AI-built presentations.","Pick what the audience must understand—then pick the motion.","Most AI presentation tools decide layout first and sprinkle animation on top. Motion Atlas reverses that order. It starts with the audience’s cognitive job—reveal, compare, connect, scale, focus, prove—then routes the scene to a motion contract with an explicit use case and an explicit “avoid when” condition."],"features":["the meaning the motion carries;","when it becomes noise;","its trigger, fallback, reduced-motion behavior, dependencies, and primary sources."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kosmoray/dayan-motion-atlas/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"48773acda8310d4bc046ee0621a86ef95b2091c64a26787d2ce0beb2d08fc278","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:21.045Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:21.045Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A visual decision system for AI-built presentations.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kosmoray/dayan-motion-atlas/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"48773acd